e, or network dependency:\n\n- **Dependencies**: `pfl-basic`, `org.ow2.asm:asm`, `org.ow2.asm:asm-util` are all plain compile-scope transitive dependencies of `pfl-dynamic` — Gradle resolves them automatically from the coordinate alone. `jakarta.ejb-api` and `junit` are test-scope deps of the upstream library itself, not needed by consumers.\n- **Runtime behavior**: Its core feature (`ObjectCopierFactory`/`ClassCopierOrdinaryImpl`) uses `sun.misc.Unsafe` and `sun.reflect.ReflectionFactory` via `pfl-basic`'s `Bridge` class — both live in the `jdk.unsupported` module, which is exported unconditionally to the unnamed module (classpath), so no `--add-opens`/`--add-exports` flags are needed on JDK 25.\n- Old `SecurityManager` permission checks (`RuntimePermission(\"reflectionFactoryAccess\")`, etc.) are no-ops since JDK 24 removed the Security Manager, so no policy file is needed either.\n- An optional experimental code-gen-based copier is gated behind `Boolean.getBoolean(\"org.glassfish.dynamic.codegen.UseCodegenReflectiveCopyobject\")`, defaulting to `false` — the default Unsafe-based copier path is what tests would exercise, no property needed for meaningful coverage.\n- No Docker image or external service is involved anywhere in the library.\n\nI found no concrete evidence that setup beyond the normal generated scaffold is needed.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"action\": \"no_action\",\n  \"summary\": \"pfl-dynamic is a standalone bytecode-generation/object-copying utility with only ordinary transitive Maven dependencies (pfl-basic, asm, asm-util) that Gradle resolves automatically. It uses sun.misc.Unsafe/sun.reflect.ReflectionFactory, which live in the always-exported jdk.unsupported module, so no extra JVM flags, Docker image, or system property is required to reach meaningful coverage on JDK 25.\",\n  \"deterministic_setup\": [],\n  \"agent_guidance\": \"Optional, not required: the default reflective/Unsafe object copier is exercised without any special setup. If a test also